<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-commitment-chase</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 1700 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' /Users/richardwhite/berwilson-platform/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/commitment-chase</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Weekdays at 5:30am — compose the follow-up for what others owe us.

    ⚠ THE SLOT IS A CORRECTNESS CONSTRAINT. LM Studio serves ONE request at a
    time and nothing in this repo queues; this makes up to a dozen sequential
    calls, so it must finish before the morning block rather than overlap it:

      04:30  lead sweep       (long, many calls)
      05:30  THIS             (<=12 short calls, ~3 sentences each)
      06:30  weekly brief     (Mondays only)
      06:50  Pepper's note    (one call per person)
      07:00  daily digest     (one call)

    5:30 is after the lead sweep's own window and an hour clear of the brief.
    The cap of 12 is what keeps it inside that hour; the rest arrive tomorrow,
    which for an obligation already three weeks old costs nothing.

    AND IT RUNS BEFORE THE NOTE ON PURPOSE: a chase composed at 05:30 is on the
    ledger page by the time the 06:50 note points the reader at it.

    Nothing here sends. The pass writes a draft or stores the text, and the
    person sends it — see src/lib/commitments/chase.ts for why storing is the
    normal outcome rather than the fallback.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/richardwhite/Library/Logs/berwilson/cron-commitment-chase.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/richardwhite/Library/Logs/berwilson/cron-commitment-chase.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
